  <compounddef id="classllvm_1_1unique__function" kind="class" language="C++" prot="public">
    <compoundname>llvm::unique_function</compoundname>
    <templateparamlist>
      <param>
        <type>typename FunctionT</type>
      </param>
    </templateparamlist>
    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1unique__function" kindref="compound">unique_function</ref> is a type-erasing functor similar to std::function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It can hold move-only function objects, like lambdas capturing unique_ptrs. Accordingly, it is movable but not copyable.</para>
<para>It supports const-qualification:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1unique__function" kindref="compound">unique_function&lt;int() const&gt;</ref> has a const operator(). It can only hold functions which themselves have a const operator().</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1unique__function" kindref="compound">unique_function&lt;int()&gt;</ref> has a non-const operator(). It can hold functions with a non-const operator(), like mutable lambdas. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
